: \"PASS\",\n      \"substitution\": \"Parent normal/emergency finally: latch no-more-output/spawn, bounded own-session APIs<=0.20s on already proven Keep-Alive only, close all lanes and lifeline_w (always finally), os.killpg(child_pgid,SIGTERM),grace<=0.50s,then os.killpg(child_pgid,SIGKILL) for whole shared helper+serve+descendant group even if serve exited. Parent reaps helper_proc, helper reaps serve_proc; total remainder<=0.50s includes joins+owned root then lease removal; aggregate<=1.20s. Parent death bypasses finally ->helper EOF plus terminal_quiescence, startup reaper for retained manifests; no new group/ambiguous proc. EVD-055 justifies killing descendants after leader exit.\",\n      \"oracle\": \"VER-005 GroupB inject parent SIGKILL (1) immediately after helper Popen before helper entry/lease, (2) immediately after serve Popen before serve_pid publication, (3) after atomic lease before handshake, (4) after handshake before lsof/READY, (5) during prompt. Same helper→serve group; EOF never lost, helper watcher active before READY. Include TERM-ignoring descendant and terminal_quiescence order (all writers stopped ->owned root removal ->lease unlink ->final same-group KILL; no imagined helper finally after self-KILL). Assert listener_pid==serve_pid and pgid==child_pgid,0 owned helper/serve/descendants/lease/temp roots,0 foreign signals/deletions including PID/PGID reuse. Separately kill/disable helper, restart bridge with retained lease ->safe startup reaper; this is recovery scenario, not immediate EOF success.50 normal cancellation cycles return all counters/FD/thread/pipe counts to0; lifeline_w closed every exit. Stage3/H0/H9 remain NOT_RUN.\",\n      \"verification_ids\": [\n        \"VER-005\"\n      ],\n      \"helper_cli_contract\": \"Helper argv=[sys.executable, \\\"-I\\\", str(Path(__file__).resolve()), \\\"--serve-helper\\\", attempt_id, str(port), ...]; start_new_session=True, child_pgid=helper_proc.pid. CLI dispatcher is inside if __name__ == \